message: "If you use this specification, please cite it as below."
title: "I-Lang Protocol Specification"
abstract: >-
  I-Lang is an AI-native communication protocol that defines a formal vocabulary
  of 88 verbs, 29 core modifiers plus a 20-key media profile, 25 entities
  (17 addressable, 8 role), and 13 Greek aliases for structured communication
  between humans and AI, between AI agents, and within AI internal
  reasoning. It introduces two syntaxes: operation syntax for executable
  instructions and declaration syntax for behavioral identity. v3.0 defines
  communication format, v4.0 adds execution semantics, and v5.0 adds a trainable
  judgment layer built on an 11-dimensional judgment vector space. v4.1
  registers image, video and audio generation intent as a target-gated modifier
  profile and a dedicated artifact entity tier.
type: software
